  "narrative": "The new evidence strengthens the MSI-high reversal and gives a nuanced picture of the central dependency landscape inside and outside MSI-high cells. Under the signed convention, H122, H123, and H126 show MSI-high cells with substantially lower, more negative dependency_composite values, meaning stronger composite dependency: adenocarcinoma signed +0.742 with interval +0.605 to +0.878; high-quality screens signed +0.748 with interval +0.605 to +0.891; high mutation burden signed +0.768 with interval +0.599 to +0.936. These effects are far above the 0.15-unit threshold, with lower bounds well above threshold, so I accept and close these context-robustness claims. They make it unlikely that the main MSI-high association is confined to a single lineage, screen-quality stratum, or mutation-burden stratum. \n\nThe interaction results mostly argue against large claimed-direction effect modification but should not be read as equivalence. H127 tests whether high mutation burden modifies the MSI-high association; the signed estimate is -0.083, interval -0.310 to +0.143, and the upper bound is below threshold for the claimed direction. I reject H127 as a direction-specific claim, while noting the interval does not exclude smaller or opposite modifications. H131 similarly rejects a claimed interaction with central-loss-intact status: signed -0.069, interval -0.276 to +0.139, with upper bound below threshold. These are not definitive proof that the MSI-high effect is invariant, but they do not support a threshold-level modification in the registered directions. \n\nThe MSI-stratified interactions are underpowered because MSI-high cells are small. H132, the KEAP1-by-MSI interaction, is signed -0.049 with a wide interval -0.300 to +0.201. Its interval includes possible threshold-level positive modification, so I leave it unresolved and close it as low priority; however, H135 directly estimates KEAP1 loss within MSI-high as signed +0.794, interval +0.552 to +1.037, which accepts and supports the KEAP1 weaker-dependency association inside MSI-high cells. H133, the SMARCA4-by-MSI interaction in the registered direction, is rejected: signed -0.181, interval -0.404 to +0.041; the upper bound is below the claimed threshold, although the raw attenuation estimate is imprecise and should not be treated as established effect modification. H136 directly estimates SMARCA4 loss within MSI-high as signed +0.658, interval +0.445 to +0.871, accepting the SMARCA4 stronger-dependency association inside MSI-high cells. H134 and H137 remain unresolved: the TP53-by-MSI interaction is wide, and the direct TP53 estimate within MSI-high is +0.301 but interval -0.129 to +0.732, crossing zero. I do not reject the TP53 effect in MSI-high; I only say the supplied MSI-high stratum is too imprecise to accept it. \n\nH138 tests PTEN loss in MSI-negative cells and gives signed +0.234, interval +0.138 to +0.331. The lower bound is just below threshold, but the point estimate is clearly meaningful, the interval excludes zero, and PTEN's main effect is already accepted and independently validated. I accept H138 and close it, interpreting it as evidence that PTEN's stronger-dependency association remains when the small MSI-high subgroup is excluded. Overall, the accepted landscape is broadening: KEAP1 and TP53 loss track with weaker composite dependency, SMARCA4 and PTEN loss track with stronger composite dependency, and MSI-high tracks strongly with stronger composite dependency. KEAP1 and SMARCA4 effects also remain direct-supported within MSI-high cells, while TP53 within MSI-high remains underpowered. \n\nI request independent validation for H120, the main reverse MSI-high claim, because it is the most important new within-dataset discovery and validation can provide an independent conservative interval. I do not validate small MSI-high sub-contexts such as H135-H137; those would likely be underpowered and would not test the primary association as efficiently. For follow-up, I register central-predictor tests within MSI-negative cells to check that the accepted central landscape is not driven by overlap with the rare MSI-high subgroup, and I retain the already-registered lineage interaction H125 for possible follow-up. I avoid additional over-stratified MSI-high subcontexts because of cell-count constraints. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal effects, single-gene knockout effects, or claims of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 appraise update: Accepted core landscape is KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss associated with weaker composite dependency (higher/less negative dependency_composite), SMARCA4 loss and PTEN loss associated with stronger composite dependency (lower/more negative dependency_composite). MSI-high accepted reverse: MSI-high associated with stronger composite dependency. Direct evidence: H120 overall signed +0.792 (accepted active, validation requested); H121 central-loss-intact signed +0.754 (accepted active); H122 adenocarcinoma signed +0.742 (accepted closed); H123 high-quality screens signed +0.748 (accepted closed); H126 high mutation burden signed +0.768 (accepted closed). Interaction robustness: H127 high-burden interaction and H131 central-loss-intact interaction rejected direction-specific because signed upper bounds are below threshold; this is not proof of no interaction but gives no support for large claimed modification. MSI-stratified central effects: H135 KEAP1 within MSI-high accepted signed +0.794; H136 SMARCA4 within MSI-high accepted signed +0.658; H137 TP53 within MSI-high unresolved/closed due wide interval. Interactions by MSI: H132 KEAP1 unresolved/closed underpowered; H133 SMARCA4 claimed direction rejected but raw attenuation imprecise; H134 TP53 unresolved/closed underpowered. PTEN in MSI-negative accepted signed +0.234, lower near but point/validated main effect support. Validation request: H120 main MSI-high reverse association. Next priorities: run TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 in MSI-negative contexts to check central landscape not driven by MSI-high overlap; consider H125 lineage-subtype interaction; avoid additional small MSI-high subcontexts. All findings remain supplied-dataset associations only, not causal or generalizable.",
